"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Concave up regions of a quartic","prompt":"Find the values of $x$ for which $y=x^{4}-6x^{2}$ is concave up.","answerType":"interval","answer":{"region":"x < -1 or x > 1","variable":"x"},"hints":["Differentiate twice.","Concave up means y″ > 0.","Solve the inequality."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Differentiate twice.","method":"Concave up means y″ > 0.","worked":"Solve the inequality."},"steps":[{"h":"Second derivative","d":"$y''=12x^{2}-12>0$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$x^{2}>1$"}],"traps":[{"region":"-1 < x < 1","why":"That is concave down."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"y″ = 12x² − 12","line":"12*x^2-12"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct region","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-C3-030","group":"A12-C3-030","dp":"C3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Open box with least surface area","prompt":"An open box with a square base of side $x$ cm has volume $32\\text{ cm}^3$. Show that its surface area is $S=x^{2}+\\dfrac{128}{x}$ and find the minimum surface area.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":48},"hints":["Open means no top face.","Differentiate S.","Check it is a minimum."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Open means no top face.","method":"Differentiate S.","worked":"Check it is a minimum."},"steps":[{"h":"Height","d":"$h=\\tfrac{32}{x^{2}}$; $S=x^{2}+4xh=x^{2}+\\tfrac{128}{x}$"},{"h":"Minimise","d":"$S'=2x-\\tfrac{128}{x^{2}}=0\\Rightarrow x=4$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$16+32=48$; $S''>0$"}],"traps":[{"value":64,"why":"Included a lid."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Shows S","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 4","line":"x = 4"},{"marks":1,"point":"48 cm²","answer":true}],"stepcheck":{"kind":"equation","variable":"x","solutions":[4]}},{"id":"A12-C3-031","group":"A12-C3-031","dp":"C3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Closest point on a root curve","prompt":"Find the point on $y=\\sqrt x$ that is closest to $(3,0)$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":2.5,"y":1.5811388300841898},"hints":["Minimise D² instead of D.","y² = x."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Minimise D² instead of D.","method":"y² = x."},"steps":[{"h":"Square distance","d":"$D^{2}=(x-3)^{2}+x$"},{"h":"Minimise","d":"$2(x-3)+1=0\\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac52$"},{"h":"Point","d":"$\\left(\\tfrac52,\\sqrt{\\tfrac52}\\right)$"}],"traps":[{"point":[3,"sqrt(3)"],"why":"That is directly above (3, 0), not closest."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"D² = (x − 3)² + x","line":"D^2 = (x-3)^2+x"},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 5/2","line":"x = 5/2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct point","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-C3-032","group":"A12-C3-032","dp":"C3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Lowest point of x ln x","prompt":"Find the minimum turning point of $y=x\\ln x$ for $x>0$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":0.36787944117144233,"y":-0.36787944117144233},"hints":["Product rule.","Solve ln x = −1.","Check y″."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Product rule.","method":"Solve ln x = −1.","worked":"Check y″."},"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$y'=\\ln x+1=0\\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac1e$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$\\tfrac1e\\ln\\tfrac1e=-\\tfrac1e$; $y''=\\tfrac1x>0$"}],"traps":[{"point":["exp(-1)","exp(-1)"],"why":"ln(1/e) = −1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = 1/e","line":"x = 1/e"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct point","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-C3-034","group":"A12-C3-034","dp":"C3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Fencing beside a river","prompt":"A rectangular field of area $800\\text{ m}^2$ has one side along a straight river, which needs no fence. Find the least length of fencing needed.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":80},"hints":["Only three sides need fencing.","Write F in one variable."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Only three sides need fencing.","method":"Write F in one variable."},"steps":[{"h":"Length","d":"Sides $x$, $x$ and $\\tfrac{800}{x}$: $F=2x+\\tfrac{800}{x}$"},{"h":"Minimise","d":"$F'=2-\\tfrac{800}{x^{2}}=0\\Rightarrow x=20$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$40+40=80$"}],"traps":[{"value":113.14,"why":"Fenced all four sides."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"F = 2x + 800/x","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 20","line":"x = 20"},{"marks":1,"point":"80 m","answer":true}],"stepcheck":{"kind":"equation","variable":"x","solutions":[20],"rejected":[-20]}},{"id":"A12-C3-036","group":"A12-C3-036","dp":"C3.1b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Point of inflection","prompt":"Find the point of inflection of $y=x^{3}-3x^{2}+2$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":1,"y":0},"hints":["Differentiate twice.","Check the concavity changes."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Differentiate twice.","method":"Check the concavity changes."},"steps":[{"h":"Second derivative","d":"$y''=6x-6=0\\Rightarrow x=1$, sign changes"},{"h":"Point","d":"$y=1-3+2=0$"}],"traps":[{"point":[0,2],"why":"That is a stationary point (y′ = 0)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = 1 with sign change","line":"x = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"(1, 0)","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-C3-039","group":"A12-C3-039","dp":"C3.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Largest cylinder in a sphere","prompt":"A cylinder of height $h$ is inscribed in a sphere of radius $3$, as shown. Find the maximum volume of the cylinder.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":65.29677711243184},"hints":["Use Pythagoras from the centre to a rim point.","Write V in terms of h."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Use Pythagoras from the centre to a rim point.","method":"Write V in terms of h."},"steps":[{"h":"Constraint","d":"$r^{2}+\\tfrac{h^{2}}{4}=9$"},{"h":"Volume","d":"$V=\\pi\\left(9h-\\tfrac{h^{3}}{4}\\right)$, $V'=\\pi\\left(9-\\tfrac{3h^{2}}{4}\\right)=0\\Rightarrow h=2\\sqrt3$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$V=\\pi(18\\sqrt3-6\\sqrt3)=12\\sqrt3\\pi$"}],"traps":[{"value":113.09733552923255,"why":"Used r = 3 for the cylinder.","expr":"36*pi"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"r² = 9 − h²/4","line":"r^2 = 9-h^2/4"},{"marks":1,"point":"h = 2√3","line":"h = 2*sqrt(3)"},{"marks":1,"point":"12√3π","answer":true}],"diagram":{"alt":"1 circle is drawn. Labels include: h, r. Read the question for what it asks.","w":160.75,"h":136.6,"sha256":"53f43e5377987e262845b5a2a2a42bbcd5bff03607e1a7db2d8f3644c217b859","bytes":4608}},{"id":"A12-C3-040","group":"A12-C3-040","dp":"C3.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Cheapest batch size","prompt":"The average cost per item is $C(x)=x+\\dfrac{100}{x}$ dollars for $x>0$. Find the minimum average cost.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":20},"hints":["Solve C′ = 0.","Substitute back."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Solve C′ = 0.","method":"Substitute back."},"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$C'=1-\\tfrac{100}{x^{2}}=0\\Rightarrow x=10$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$C(10)=20$; $C''>0$"}],"traps":[{"value":10,"why":"Gave x, not C."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = 10","line":"x = 10"},{"marks":1,"point":"20 dollars","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-C3-043","group":"A12-C3-043","dp":"C3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Rectangle under a parabola","prompt":"A rectangle has one corner at the origin and the opposite corner on $y=12-x^{2}$ in the first quadrant, as shown. Find its maximum area.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":16},"hints":["Width x and height 12 − x².","Check it is a maximum."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Width x and height 12 − x².","method":"Check it is a maximum."},"steps":[{"h":"Area","d":"$A=x(12-x^{2})$"},{"h":"Maximise","d":"$A'=12-3x^{2}=0\\Rightarrow x=2$"},{"h":"Value","d":"$2\\times8=16$"}],"traps":[{"value":32,"why":"Used width 2x as if symmetric about the y-axis."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"A = x(12 − x²)","line":"A = x*(12-x^2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 2","line":"x = 2"},{"marks":1,"point":"16","answer":true}],"diagram":{"alt":"Graph drawn on x and y axes; 1 plotted line, curve or set of points is drawn. Marked on the horizontal axis: 2; vertical axis: 8, 12. Read the question for what it asks.","w":186.68,"h":156.89,"sha256":"ae58fe6016029f83be236064da8b2cb4ff0cff120c0473eec2a828b0de7af7e9","bytes":6749}},{"id":"A12-C3-044","group":"A12-C3-044","dp":"C3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Least velocity","